{%- capture direction -%}{% render 'direction' %}{%- endcapture -%}
<!doctype html>
<html class="no-js" lang="{{ request.locale.iso_code }}" dir="{{ direction }}">
  <head>


{% render 'replo-head' %}
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta http-equiv="X-UA-Compatible" content="IE=edge,chrome=1">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
    <meta name="theme-color" content="{{ settings.color_button_background }}">

    {%- comment -%}
      Intelligems must run before first paint to avoid variant flicker, so it
      sits as high as possible — after <meta charset> (which has to land in the
      first 1024 bytes) and before everything else. The preconnect has to stay
      directly above it or it buys nothing: the script is render-blocking, so
      its DNS + TLS handshake is on the critical path.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://cdn.intelligems.io" crossorigin>
    {% render 'intelligems' %}

    <link rel="canonical" href="{{ canonical_url }}">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://cdn.shopify.com" crossorigin>
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.shopifycdn.com" crossorigin>
    {% # theme-check-disable RemoteAsset %}
    <link rel="dns-prefetch" href="https://ajax.googleapis.com">
    <link rel="dns-prefetch" href="https://maps.googleapis.com">
    <link rel="dns-prefetch" href="https://maps.gstatic.com">
    {% # theme-check-enable RemoteAsset %}
    {% render 'inf-header-scripts' %}

    {%- if settings.favicon != blank -%}
      <link rel="shortcut icon" href="{{ settings.favicon | image_url: width: 32, height: 32 }}" type="image/png">
    {%- endif -%}

    <title>
      {{- page_title -}}
      {%- if current_tags -%}
        {%- assign meta_tags = current_tags | join: ', ' %} &ndash; {{ 'general.meta.tags' | t: tags: meta_tags -}}
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if current_page != 1 %} &ndash; {{ 'general.meta.page' | t: page: current_page }}{% endif -%}
      {%- if request.page_type == 'password' -%}
        {{- shop.name -}}
      {%- else -%}
        {%- unless page_title contains shop.name %} &ndash; {{ shop.name }}{% endunless -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    </title>

    {%- if page_description -%}
      <meta name="description" content="{{ page_description | escape }}">
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- liquid
      render 'social-meta-tags'

      render 'css-variables'
      echo 'theme.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag: preload: true

      if direction == 'rtl'
        echo 'rtl.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag: preload: true
      endif
    -%}

    <link
      rel="stylesheet"
      href="{{ 'apps.css' | asset_url }}"
      media="print"
      fetchpriority="low"
      onload="this.media='all'"
    >
    {% comment %}  {{ 'custom.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}   {% endcomment %}

    {%- comment -%}
      custom-jtpl.css deferred 2026-08-09.

      Lighthouse measured this file at 1,650ms of render-blocking time — the
      single largest blocking stylesheet on the site.

      Safe to defer because it is almost entirely below-the-fold styling. Every
      one of its 230 top-level rules was tested against the above-the-fold DOM
      of five templates (home, product, collection, cart, blog). The same and
      only 2 rules can match up there on every template:

        html { scroll-behavior: smooth }        -> behavioural, not paint
        .rtx-subscription input:…:after { … }   -> inside the hidden cart drawer

      Neither affects first paint, so nothing flashes. `scroll-behavior` is
      inlined below so smooth scrolling is live immediately rather than after
      the deferred fetch.

      The noscript fallback matches the pattern already used by blog.css and
      mobile-dock.css elsewhere in this theme.

      If a future edit adds above-the-fold rules to this file, they will paint
      late. Re-run the above-fold rule test before assuming it is still safe.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <style>html{scroll-behavior:smooth}</style>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ 'custom-jtpl.css' | asset_url }}" media="print" onload="this.media='all'">
    <noscript>{{ 'custom-jtpl.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}</noscript>

    {%- comment -%}
      recipekit.css (7,989 B) styles the RecipeKit app block, which is rendered
      only by sections/main-article-overlay.liquid — and that section is used
      only by article.*.json templates. It was loading render-blocking on every
      page: home, product, collection, cart, account. Now scoped to articles.

      If RecipeKit is ever added to a page or product template, widen this
      condition or the recipe card will render unstyled. Nothing warns you.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if request.page_type == 'article' -%}
      {{ 'recipekit.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
    {%- endif -%}

    {{ content_for_header }}

    {%if template contains "product" and product.tags contains "hidden" %}
      <script> window.location.href ="/" ;</script>
      {%endif %}

