         Vendor default injects heatmap.min.js during head parsing. That loader
         immediately pulls dashboard.heatmap.com/heatmap-light.min.js, which the
         Forced Reflow audit measured at 348ms of layout thrashing — more than
         every other script on the page combined — landing squarely inside Total
         Blocking Time.

         The cheap parts of the snippet (queue, tracker URL, global error
         listeners) still run inline so no early errors are lost. Only the
         script injection is moved to browser idle time after first paint.

         To revert, restore the one-line vendor snippet from git history:
           git log -S"_heatmap_paq" -- layout/theme.liquid
      */
